FINAL ANSWER:
Status: `git blame` finished on every tracked file, and I'm writing up the result.

I didn't use the `busfactor` script for this answer. It scores commits with a decay over time, which is closer to "who has been active" than to "whose lines survive". Its dry-run also produced a fallback owner list that includes `fiona@formatter.example`, the account behind the latest reformat commit. I'd treat that output as unreliable until it's checked.

**Method:** I ran `git blame -w -M -C` on all 18 tracked files, skipping lockfiles and images. I told blame to ignore `62628c0`, the 2026-04-12 reformat commit. Without that, Fiona Formatter would own 291 lines, which are only whitespace and quote changes.

**Who owns the surviving lines** (about 2,000 lines in total, so percentages are approximate):

| Author | Surviving lines | Share |
|---|---|---|
| Troy Goode | 810 | ~40% |
| Douglas Christopher Wilson | 629 | ~30% |
| Íñigo Marquínez Prado | 95 | ~5% |
| Jon Church | 72 | ~3% |
| Sebastian Beltran | 67 | ~3% |
| Ulises Gascón | 52 | ~3% |
| Ignacio Mangas | 44 | ~2% |

The remaining ~14% is spread across about 38 other people, most with fewer than 30 lines each.

**By area:**
- **`lib/index.js`:** Troy has 159 lines and Douglas has 22. Most of Troy's lines come from older commits (`4f13c63`, `8ec22a9`), not his recent work.
- **`test/*`:** Troy and Douglas split `test/test.js` almost evenly, 317 lines to 339. Troy owns most of the other test files, and all 36 lines of `test/vary.js`.
- **`README.md`:** Troy has 116 lines and Jon Church has 72.
- **`.github/workflows` and `dependabot.yml`:** These belong to recent maintainers: Douglas (118 lines in `ci.yml`), Ignacio Mangas, Sebastian Beltran, Íñigo Marquínez and Ulises Gascón.
- **`HISTORY.md`, `.eslintrc.yml`, `LICENSE`:** These are mostly Douglas's.

**Caveats:**
- **Imported history.** The history starts in 2013 with one bulk commit of 8 files. Blame credits the author recorded in that history, which may not be whoever originally wrote the code.
- **Troy's two recent commits.** Troy also made `b2005d9` (12 lines in `lib/index.js`) and `02afce3` (the new `test/vary.js`) on 2026-04-10. His share would be about 10% lower, ~30% instead of ~40%, if his older code turns out to be a mass import and not his own writing. I haven't checked that.
- **Who is still active.** Blame shows whose lines remain, not who is still around to maintain them. I haven't checked who is active, so I can't say which of these areas are orphaned.
- **Re-attribution.** `-C` credits moved or copied lines to their original author. I haven't tried a run without it.

Next, I can run the full `busfactor` report with `--no-github`, check which authors are active, and give you the orphaned and bus-factor-1 zones. Say if you want that.

